project or its contributors.

Murage's common ancestor with OpenMausBot is the 0.1.44 source (commit
6140532e). Everything after that point is selective adaptation, not parity.
Murage does not import whole upstream releases, and no upstream release
should be described as having been imported into Murage.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
WhatsApp channel
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The WhatsApp channel links the user's own WhatsApp account through Baileys
(https://github.com/WhiskeySockets/Baileys, npm package "baileys" 7.0.0-rc14),
Copyright (c) 2025 Rajeh Taher/WhiskeySockets, licensed under the MIT License
(third_party/baileys/LICENSE). Baileys depends on libsignal 6.0.0, licensed
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (third_party/libsignal-node/
LICENSE); GPL-3.0 is compatible with this product's AGPL-3.0-or-later and its
full text accompanies the distribution. Baileys, jimp and their dependencies
are shipped unmodified under server/node_modules; each package's licence is
recorded in whatsapp-runtime-manifest.json.

Portions of the channel are adapted from Hermes Agent scripts/whatsapp-bridge,
Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research (MIT, third_party/hermes-agent/LICENSE), and
from OpenClaw extensions/whatsapp, Copyright (c) 2026 OpenClaw Foundation
(MIT, third_party/openclaw/LICENSE).

Murage is not affiliated with, authorized, endorsed by, or in any way
officially connected with WhatsApp or any of its subsidiaries or affiliates.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Muse Code engine
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Murage talks to a Muse Code CLI the owner installs from Meta through the
Muse Session Protocol SDK (https://github.com/meta-models/muse-code-sdk, npm
package "@muse-code/sdk" 1.4.14), Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and
affiliates, licensed under the MIT License (third_party/muse-code-sdk/
LICENSE). The Muse Code CLI itself is not part of this distribution: Murage
never ships, mirrors or installs it. Meta's terms apply to its use.

Murage is not affiliated with, authorized, endorsed by, or in any way
officially connected with Meta Platforms, Inc.

